  "_hooks_note": [
    "The Bearing plugin ships the standard hooks (format edited file, block",
    "publish commands, inject task id, session start summary, stop reminder).",
    "A repository whose make check runs under two minutes may add a heavier Stop",
    "hook here that runs it. Measure first; a slow hook on every stop is worse",
    "than no hook."
  ],
  "_sandbox_note": "OS-enforced boundary for every Bash command the agent runs (Seatbelt on macOS; bubblewrap and socat on Linux and WSL2). Network is an allowlist of package registries only: the git host, cloud APIs and deploy endpoints are absent, so a push or a deploy fails at the network layer whatever the command string looks like. Credentials stay unreadable. Add a registry your stack needs in .claude/settings.local.json; arrays merge. doctor checks the Linux prerequisites. Writes go to the repository, the session $TMPDIR (/tmp itself is read-only by design) and the package caches in filesystem.allowWrite, so npm, pnpm, uv, pip, go and gradle can install; make harness-eval's sandbox scenario proves both halves.",
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": false,
    "failIfUnavailable": true,
    "autoAllowBashIfSandboxed": false,
    "allowUnsandboxedCommands": false,
    "network": {
      "allowedDomains": [
        "registry.npmjs.org",
        "*.npmjs.org",
        "registry.yarnpkg.com",
        "pypi.org",
        "files.pythonhosted.org",
        "proxy.golang.org",
